## Setup and commands

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .            # plus dev tools from pyproject / requirements-dev.txt
pytest                      # tests
black --check . && flake8   # lint
pre-commit run --all-files  # all hooks
```

## Code style

- Type hints on all function signatures
- Google-style docstrings on public functions
- Formatting: `black` (line-length 88) + `flake8`
- Tests: `pytest` for all behavior changes
{% if profile == "system" %}

## Discovery-driven development

- Run `./scripts/discovery.sh` before proposing changes.
- **Ansible-first**: no manual `apt`/`pip` installs. Port changes to Ansible roles.
{% else %}

## Discovery-driven development

- Check existing code in `src/` before proposing changes.
- Search for existing implementations before creating new utility functions.
- Check `pyproject.toml` before adding new dependencies.
{% endif %}

## Git workflow

- **`main`**: production-ready code, releases only. Never commit to it directly.
- **`develop`**: integration branch; all work merges here.
- Short-lived local branches off `develop`: `feat/`, `fix/`, `docs/`, `chore/`.
- Merge back into `develop` (`--squash` for one clean commit, or `--no-ff`),
  delete the branch, then push `develop`. Merge `develop` into `main` with
  `--no-ff` for releases.
- Run tests before merging. Ask before pushing (`git push origin` needs explicit
  user approval).
- Conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`),
  imperative mood, subject under 72 characters.

## neo-harness (if embedded)

If `scripts/neo` or `requirements-neo.txt` exists, bounded PLAN→ACT→REFLECT jobs
prefer the workspace runner over free-form chat:

```bash
./scripts/neo doctor
./scripts/neo start --task-file jobs/<slug>.md --agent workspace -p mock
```

See [neo-harness starting-a-workspace](https://github.com/westailabs/neo-harness/blob/master/docs/starting-a-workspace.md).

## Hard rules

- Do not commit secrets or `.env`
- Do not invent service health without a probe
- Prefer tests for behavior changes
